      "math_academy_id": "q-95993",
      "problem": "Given $X∼\\text{Po}(2),$ compute $P(X=3),$ rounded to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Po}(\\lambda ),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Po}(2),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{2}^{x}{e}^{-2}}{x!}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =f(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{3}{e}^{-2}}{3!} \\\\  & ≈0.1804.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
